# Implements port slice 2 (A2; q37): inside `apply`, `op` is called with two inputs where its header
# written in place takes one -- refused at that call, "incompatible entry signature" (the needle pins
# its place: before A2 the phrase was said at the header).
fn: inc (int: x) int
    return: x + 1
end: inc

fn: apply (op(fn: (int: x) int) int(value)) int
    return: op(value value)
end: apply

int: ok 7
if: apply(inc 10) != 11
    ok: 1
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
